walkthrough "pearos - the NiceC0re installer, on ext4"
resolution 1920x1080
recording_resolution 1920x1080
var out
  default out/distro.qcow2
  from args.out

# NO `password` AND NO `user` HERE, AND THAT IS NOT AN OMISSION. Every other Linux walk declares both
# because its installer asks for them; this one has no account page at all, so declaring a password
# would name a credential nothing on the disk holds. The account is created by pearOS on first boot.


# pearOS IS A CALAMARES INSTALLER, BUT IT REACHES IT THROUGH TWO PAGES NO OTHER CALAMARES MEDIUM HERE
# HAS, AND ITS CALAMARES HAS NO `Users` PAGE AT ALL.
#
# MEASURED by driving the whole install by hand to `All done. / 100%`, on a 40 GiB disk:
#
#	desktop          click `Install pearOS`
#	Language         the wrapper's own page, English preselected, an ARROW bottom-right
#	Recovery         a macOS-style chooser: `Restore from Time Machine`, `Install pearOS NiceC0re`,
#	                 `Web Browser`, `GParted`, and a `Continue` button
#	Welcome          Calamares begins here
#	Location         Asia/Tokyo preselected
#	Keyboard         English (US)/Default preselected
#	Partitions       NOTHING is selected, so Next is disabled until `Erase disk` is chosen
#	Summary          ext4 is the default file system - the partition table it drew was
#	                 300 MiB FAT32 (EFI) + 39.71 GiB ext4, no swap
#	Install          5 -> 11 -> 19 -> 58 -> 75 -> 88 -> 100%, about nine minutes
#	Finish          `All done.` and a `Done` button
#
# THERE IS NO USER PAGE. The account is created by pearOS on first boot, which is why this walk has no
# user form to fill - and why the ssh stage is a separate question rather than a formality.


step "the media this stage boots from is already on disk"
  needs [pearos.iso]


# FORTY GIB, WHICH IS THE SIZE THE HAND RUN USED AND THE SIZE THE SUMMARY REPORTED BACK.
step "create the empty disk"
  disk
    file disk.qcow2
    size 40


step "boot the installer"
  boot
    machine "q35,accel=kvm,vmport=off"
    args [["-cpu", "Skylake-Client-v4"], ["-smp", "4"], ["-drive", "if=pflash,format=raw,readonly=on,file=/usr/share/OVMF/OVMF_CODE_4M.fd"], ["-drive", "if=pflash,format=raw,file=OVMF_VARS.fd"], ["-m", "4096"], ["-chardev", "socket,id=qga0,path=qga.sock,server=on,wait=off"], ["-device", "virtio-serial"], ["-device", "virtserialport,chardev=qga0,name=org.qemu.guest_agent.0"], ["-device", "VGA,xres=1920,yres=1080,vgamem_mb=32"], ["-device", "qemu-xhci,id=xhci"], ["-device", "usb-tablet,bus=xhci.0"], ["-device", "usb-kbd,bus=xhci.0"], ["-drive", "file=pearos.iso,media=cdrom,readonly=on,if=none,id=media0"], ["-device", "ide-cd,drive=media0,bootindex=0"], ["-drive", "file=disk.qcow2,if=none,format=qcow2,id=target"], ["-device", "virtio-blk-pci,drive=target,bootindex=1"], ["-audiodev", "none,id=snd0"], ["-device", "ich9-intel-hda"], ["-device", "hda-duplex,audiodev=snd0"], ["-netdev", "tap,id=net0,ifname=qemutap0,script=no,downscript=no"], ["-device", "virtio-net-pci,netdev=net0,mac=52:54:00:56:4d:01,romfile=,host_mtu=1450"]]
    timeout 1800


# THE LIVE SESSION LANDS ON A DESKTOP AND OPENS ITS OWN WELCOME WINDOW - there is no greeter to answer.
# `Welcome` is the window's own title, and it is the first word of every frame once the panel is up.
step "the live session is at its desktop"
  repeat
    do
      item
        settle 5
      item "read the screen"
        read
          name screen
    until
      bind up
      source screen
      mode text
      rect [0, 0, 1920, 60]
      rect_at [1920, 1080]
      scale 1
      words [[Welcome]]
    max 180
    pause 4


step "open the installer, which is the welcome window's first button"
  input 893 322
  settle 25


# THE WRAPPER'S LANGUAGE PAGE. ITS `Next` IS AN ARROW IN THE BOTTOM-RIGHT CORNER, NOT A WORDED BUTTON.
step "the installer's language page"
  repeat
    do
      item
        settle 4
      item "read the screen"
        read
          name lang
    until
      bind there
      source lang
      mode text
      rect [700, 380, 1250, 620]
      rect_at [1920, 1080]
      scale 1
      words [[Language]]
    max 60
    pause 3


step "take English, which is already selected"
  input 1345 845
  settle 20


# THE RECOVERY CHOOSER. `Install pearOS NiceC0re` IS THE SECOND ROW AND `Continue` IS THE BUTTON.
#
# MEASURED: choosing the row only moves the highlight; the button is what acts, and the row that is
# already highlighted on arrival is `Restore from Time Machine` - so a walk that pressed Continue
# without choosing first would wipe nothing and install nothing.
step "the recovery chooser"
  repeat
    do
      item
        settle 4
      item "read the screen"
        read
          name rec
    until
      bind there
      source rec
      mode text
      rect [700, 320, 1240, 830]
      rect_at [1920, 1080]
      scale 1
      words [[Install, pearOS], [Restore, from, Time, Machine]]
    max 90
    pause 3


step "choose Install pearOS NiceC0re"
  input 970 481
  settle 6


step "continue into Calamares"
  input 1179 797
  settle 30


# FROM HERE IT IS CALAMARES, SO THE SAME QUESTION EVERY OTHER CALAMARES WALK ASKS: IS THE WIZARD UP?
step "Calamares is up"
  repeat
    do
      item
        settle 4
      item "read the screen"
        read
          name cal
    until
      bind up
      source cal
      mode text
      rect [600, 60, 1330, 120]
      rect_at [1920, 1080]
      scale 1
      words [[Welcome, to, the, pearOS, installer]]
    max 90
    pause 3


step "welcome - next"
  input 1777 933
  settle 18


step "location - the map already picked a zone"
  input 1777 933
  settle 18


step "keyboard - English (US) is already the layout"
  input 1777 933
  settle 30


# THE PARTITIONS PAGE ARRIVES WITH NOTHING SELECTED, AND ITS Next IS DISABLED UNTIL THE DISK IS TOLD
# WHAT TO DO. MEASURED on that frame: the radio beside `Erase disk` is empty and the pill reads
# (47,47,47); after the click the radio fills and ext4 appears as the chosen file system.
step "partitions - choose erase disk"
  input 20 104
  settle 8


step "partitions - next"
  input 1777 933
  settle 25


# THE SUMMARY IS WHERE THE FILE SYSTEM IS CONFIRMED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. It drew
# `300.00 MiB FAT32` (EFI) and `39.71 GiB ext4` (root), which is what this repository wants and what
# the medium defaults to - so nothing needs changing here, and the step only has to press Install.
step "summary - install"
  input 1757 933
  settle 30


# THE INSTALL, READ FROM THE ONE LINE THAT IS ACTUALLY LEGIBLE WHEN IT ENDS.
#
# THIS STEP USED TO WATCH A 25-PIXEL STRIP ALONG THE BOTTOM FOR THE WORD `Done`, AND THAT COST A
# FULL RUN: 83 minutes in `follow it`, then failure, while the install had finished in about twenty.
# The recording from run 45600760174 ends on a complete install - `All done. / pearOS has been
# installed on your computer. / [ ] Restart now / [Back] [Next] [Done]` - and the log shows why the
# strip never matched it:
#
#	see: 1 word(s): ES          <- progress captions, 7%, 20%, 38%, 52%, 63%
#	...
#	see: 0 word(s):             <- 159 consecutive reads of the strip, all empty
#
# The strip is blank on the progress page and its button label is too small for the reader at
# `scale 1`, so the walk waited forever on a page it had already passed. The heading is the witness:
# `All done.` is drawn large, centred, and on no other page of this installer.
#
# THE `max` COVERS THE WHOLE INSTALL, not the end of it: this step starts when `Install` is pressed
# and the unpack-and-configure phase measured about twenty minutes in CI, so 120 attempts of
# fifteen seconds is thirty minutes of headroom past what the hand run took.
step "the install runs to all done"
  repeat
    do
      item
        settle 15
      item "read the screen"
        read
          name fin
    until
      bind there
      source fin
      mode text
      rect [700, 390, 1240, 440]
      rect_at [1920, 1080]
      scale 1
      words [[All, done]]
    max 120
    pause 5


step "dismiss the finished installer"
  input 1862 933
  settle 15


# THE INSTALLER SAYS IT IS DONE BEFORE ITS BOOTLOADER IS FLUSHED.
#
# MEASURED on mint's published disk (run 45916738708): it boots to a bare `grub>` prompt although
# grub.cfg exists - a bootloader installed and its configuration not yet fsynced when `stop kill`
# terminated qemu. anduinos, popos and ubuntu pass and all of them settle twenty seconds between
# "ready to use" and the kill; this is the same wait.
step "give the installer its last few seconds, because \"done\" is not \"flushed\""
  settle 25


step "stop the machine"
  stop kill
  timeout 120


step "publish the disk"
    save "{{ out }}"
